  "findings": [
    {
      "claim": "MinecartUpdateChild clears prior rider/cart references and binds both directions; cart child offset0x318 and rider cart offset0x32c.",
      "evidence": "0x4bc2d7-0x4bc365"
    },
    {
      "claim": "SetMinecartPosVel updates position, current grid index, velocity and stored rail direction.",
      "evidence": "0x4bc1fb-0x4bc28e"
    },
    {
      "claim": "Movement projects onto rail geometry through0x939120. It samples movement in bounded substeps, queries the current tile and reverses the returned direction when the helper endpoint flag is set.",
      "evidence": "0x4bb550-0x4bb665"
    },
    {
      "claim": "Variants7/8/9/10 are endpoint segments. At along>=1 and positive incoming dot tangent, the helper sets its endpoint flag. This supports reversal when approached into the cap.",
      "evidence": "0x9391c7-0x9391df;0x939504-0x93953c"
    },
    {
      "claim": "Vertical cap9 starts at(0,13) and ends at(0,-4);10 starts at(0,-13) and ends at(0,4). Their inward ports are south and north respectively.",
      "evidence": "rail table at0xbc76f0"
    },
    {
      "claim": "The projection scores candidate segments using distance and an incoming-direction term. Straight crossing traversal is supported for centered cardinal entry, but arbitrary off-track/collision approach behavior is not claimed by a compiled route.",
      "evidence": "0x93938b-0x9394d1;crossing tablevariant6"
    }
  ],
  "limitations": [
    "Only three API signatures uniquely identify names; other function names follow local call/prologue context.",
    "The runtime curved physical path remains a declared3D adaptation; it is not a reimplementation of every native projection/collision detail.",
    "Door scheduling, bomb fuse/tick semantics, passengers and all boss attack states are not resolved by this cart excerpt."
  ]
